    "title": "COPA: Chicago cop should be fired for sexual assault, lying to investigators - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tim Hecke ,\n1 days ago A Chicago police officer has been recommended for termination after COPA sustained allegations that he sexually assaulted his then-18-year-old girlfriend, provided her with alcohol, and later accessed the police report identifying him as the suspect. Officer Alberto Rodriguez, 36, a Chicago police officer since 2014, is stripped of his police powers and assigned to a unit that takes police reports by phone at the city’s 311 call center, according to a police spokesperson. He was paid $115,158 last year. Read full article",
